multiple-choice questions for https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B

    llm.decide(state, "did the deployment succeed?", ["yes", "no", "unclear"])
    -> {"yes": 0.91, "no": 0.03, "unclear": 0.06}

with a json grammar the model still writes its answer out, token
by token, and you get back the one it wrote.

here the model writes nothing. the first forward pass already
scores every option; we read those scores and return them all.

one pass instead of several, and you see how sure it was.

https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/openjev did this with a 4B model.

quick demo:

    $ ./run.sh uv run example.py
